## 3. Architecture: How This Plugs into NIDP

The sector-aware scoring sits inside the existing `v3_scores_engine` Cloud Run job, running after `fundamental_engine` and `technical_indicator_engine` complete (post 19:00 IST in the daily chain).

```
bhavcopy ──► feature_snapshotter ──► technical_indicator_engine ──┐
                                                                   │
nse_financials ──► fundamental_engine ─────────────────────────────┤
                                                                   ▼
nse_shareholding ──────────────────────────────────────────► v3_scores_engine
                                                                   │
corporate_event_signals ───────────────────────────────────────────┤
                                                                   │
sector_master (gate) ──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                                                   │
                                                                   ▼
                                                    nidp.v3_stock_scores_daily
                                                    (sector_profile, sub_scores, final_score, band)
```

**Required schema additions to `nidp.v3_stock_scores_daily`:**

```sql
ALTER TABLE nidp.v3_stock_scores_daily
  ADD COLUMN sector_profile         VARCHAR(32),   -- BANK | NBFC | CYCLICAL | IT | FMCG | PHARMA | CAPGOODS | DEFAULT
  ADD COLUMN fundamental_score      NUMERIC(5,2),  -- 0–100, sector-weighted
  ADD COLUMN technical_score        NUMERIC(5,2),  -- 0–100
  ADD COLUMN cycle_position_score   NUMERIC(5,2),  -- 0–100, populated for CYCLICAL only
  ADD COLUMN red_flag_penalty       NUMERIC(5,2),  -- subtracted from total
  ADD COLUMN sub_scores_jsonb       JSONB,         -- nested breakdown for explainability
  ADD COLUMN final_score            NUMERIC(5,2),
  ADD COLUMN band                   VARCHAR(16);   -- STRONG_BUY | BUY | HOLD | REDUCE | AVOID
```

The `sub_scores_jsonb` column is critical — it allows the copilot to *explain* why a stock scored what it did, e.g.:

```json
{
  "asset_quality": 78, "profitability": 65, "capital_adequacy": 88,
  "growth": 60, "efficiency": 70, "valuation": 55,
  "red_flags": [{"code": "PROMOTER_PLEDGE_HIGH", "penalty": -10}]
}
```

