## 5. Sector Classification Logic

The framework maps each stock to a `sector_profile` using `nidp.sector_master`:

| `sector_master` Sector | `sector_profile` |
|---|---|
| Banks (Public Sector), Banks (Private) | `BANK` |
| Finance, NBFC, Housing Finance | `NBFC` |
| Metals & Mining, Cement, Auto & Auto Components, Chemicals, Real Estate, Construction Materials | `CYCLICAL` |
| Information Technology, Software Services | `IT` |
| FMCG, Personal Care, Consumer Staples, Tobacco | `FMCG` |
| Pharmaceuticals, Healthcare, Biotechnology | `PHARMA` |
| Capital Goods, Industrial Machinery, Infrastructure, Engineering | `CAPGOODS` |
| Everything else | `DEFAULT` (uses fallback weights) |

Conglomerates (Reliance, ITC, etc.) get a `_CONGLOMERATE` suffix and use weighted sum-of-parts when segment-level data is available.

