## 6. Sector-Specific Scoring Formulas

For each sector below: data sources, sub-score formulas, weights, and red flags are specified.

### 6.1 Banks

**Sector profile:** `BANK`
**Universe size:** ~20–25 stocks in Nifty 500

**Final Score:**

```
Final_Bank = (Fundamental × 0.70) + (Technical × 0.30) − Red_Flag_Penalty
```

**Fundamental Score (out of 100):**

```
Fundamental_Bank = 
    (Asset_Quality × 0.28) +
    (Profitability × 0.22) +
    (Capital_Adequacy × 0.15) +
    (Growth × 0.15) +
    (Efficiency × 0.10) +
    (Governance × 0.05) +
    (Valuation × 0.05)
```

#### Asset Quality (the most critical pillar)

```
Asset_Quality = 
    (GNPA_Score × 0.35) +
    (NNPA_Score × 0.35) +
    (PCR_Score × 0.20) +
    (Slippage_Score × 0.10)
```

| Metric | Formula | Source |
|---|---|---|
| GNPA_Score | LIB(GNPA%, floor=1, ceiling=5) | `nse_financials_quarterly` (bank XBRL extensions) |
| NNPA_Score | LIB(NNPA%, floor=0.3, ceiling=2) | Same |
| PCR_Score | HIB(PCR%, floor=50, ceiling=85) | Same |
| Slippage_Score | LIB(Annualized slippage %, floor=0.5, ceiling=3) | Quarterly slippage from sequential quarters |

#### Profitability

```
Profitability = 
    (NIM_Score × 0.30) +
    (RoA_Score × 0.35) +
    (RoE_Score × 0.35)
```

| Metric | Formula |
|---|---|
| NIM_Score | HIB(NIM%, floor=2.0, ceiling=4.5) |
| RoA_Score | HIB(RoA%, floor=0.5, ceiling=1.8) |
| RoE_Score | HIB(RoE%, floor=8, ceiling=20) |

#### Capital Adequacy

```
Capital_Adequacy = (CAR_Score × 0.50) + (CET1_Score × 0.50)

CAR_Score   = HIB(CAR%,  floor=11.5, ceiling=18)
CET1_Score  = HIB(CET1%, floor=8,    ceiling=15)
```

#### Growth

```
Growth = 
    (Credit_Growth_Score × 0.40) +
    (CASA_Score × 0.30) +
    (Deposit_Growth_Score × 0.30)

Credit_Growth_Score: Sector percentile rank, capped — values above 25% YoY 
                     score 70 (suggests aggressive risk-taking, not quality)
CASA_Score          = HIB(CASA%, floor=25, ceiling=50)
Deposit_Growth      = Sector percentile rank
```

#### Efficiency & Valuation

```
Efficiency = LIB(Cost_to_Income%, floor=35, ceiling=55)

Valuation_Bank = 100 − P/B_Percentile_in_own_5Y_history
```

Banks use **Price-to-Book** as the valuation anchor, not P/E. This is consumed from `nidp.stock_fundamentals_daily` (the `fundamental_engine` must extend its computations to include P/B and bank-specific ratios — see Section 11).

#### Red Flags for Banks

Sourced from `announcement_classifier` taxonomy in `nidp.corporate_announcements`:

| Red Flag (classifier category) | Penalty |
|---|---|
| `RBI_PCA_ACTION` (Prompt Corrective Action) | −25 |
| `AUDITOR_RESIGNATION` | −15 |
| `RESTRUCTURED_BOOK_SPIKE` (> 3% jump QoQ) | −15 |
| `KEY_MANAGEMENT_EXIT` (CEO/MD/CFO without succession) | −10 |
| `PROMOTER_PLEDGE` > 50% | −10 |
| `REGULATORY_PENALTY` (RBI fine > ₹10 cr) | −8 |

