### 6.3 Cyclicals (Metals, Cement, Auto, Chemicals)

**Sector profile:** `CYCLICAL`
**Critical insight:** Use through-cycle normalized earnings. P/E at the bottom of a cycle looks expensive (low E); P/E at the peak looks cheap (high E). Both are traps.

**Final Score:**

```
Final_Cyclical = (Fundamental × 0.50) + (Technical × 0.30) + (Cycle_Position × 0.20)
                 − Red_Flag_Penalty
```

The dedicated **Cycle_Position** sub-score is what distinguishes cyclical scoring from everything else.

#### Fundamental Score

```
Fundamental_Cyclical = 
    (Balance_Sheet_Strength × 0.30) +
    (Operational_Efficiency × 0.22) +
    (Through_Cycle_Profitability × 0.20) +
    (Valuation × 0.15) +
    (Free_Cash_Flow_Quality × 0.08) +
    (Governance × 0.05)
```

#### Balance Sheet Strength (cyclicals die in downturns from leverage)

```
Balance_Sheet = 
    (Debt_to_EBITDA_Score × 0.40) +
    (Interest_Coverage_Score × 0.30) +
    (Current_Ratio_Score × 0.30)

Debt_to_EBITDA_Score    = LIB(D/EBITDA, floor=0.5, ceiling=4)
Interest_Coverage_Score = HIB(IC, floor=2, ceiling=10)
Current_Ratio_Score     = HIB(CR, floor=1, ceiling=2.5)
```

All sourced from `nidp.stock_fundamentals_daily` (already computed by `fundamental_engine`).

#### Through-Cycle Profitability (use 7–10Y averages)

```
Through_Cycle = 
    (10Y_Avg_ROCE_Score × 0.50) +
    (10Y_Avg_EBITDA_Margin_Score × 0.50)

Source: Compute 10Y avgs from nidp.nse_financials_annual (requires history depth check)
For stocks listed < 10Y, use max available with minimum 5Y, flagged as PARTIAL_HISTORY
```

#### Cycle Position Score (the "secret sauce")

```
Cycle_Position = 
    (Commodity_Price_Position × 0.40) +
    (Margin_Position × 0.30) +
    (Capacity_Utilization_Position × 0.30)

Commodity_Price_Position:
    100 if relevant commodity in bottom 25% of 10Y range
    0  if in top 25%
    Linear scale in between
    
Margin_Position:
    100 if current EBITDA margin in bottom quartile of own 10Y history (compression done)
    0  if in top quartile (peak margin — likely to mean-revert down)
```

**Counter-intuitive scoring:** high score when things look operationally weak. This is what separates cyclical investing from growth investing — you're rewarded for buying when the cycle is at the trough.

> **Data gap:** Commodity price linkage requires a new feed. See Section 11 — recommend ingesting LME (metals), Platts (cement inputs), Brent (chemicals) commodity time series.

#### Cyclical Red Flags

| Red Flag | Penalty |
|---|---|
| `DEBT_COVENANT_BREACH` | −25 |
| `RATING_DOWNGRADE` | −15 |
| `CAPACITY_IMPAIRMENT_CHARGE` | −10 |
| `MASSIVE_CAPEX_AT_PEAK_CYCLE` (capex > 50% of revenue when cycle is hot) | −10 |
| `PROMOTER_PLEDGE` > 30% | −10 |

