### 6.6 Pharmaceuticals

**Sector profile:** `PHARMA`
**Critical split:** Domestic-focused vs export-heavy companies have very different risk profiles. Use export revenue % from segment disclosures to weight the sub-scores.

**Fundamental Score (export-heavy variant):**

```
Fundamental_Pharma_Export = 
    (Pipeline_Strength × 0.23) +
    (Regulatory_Standing × 0.20) +
    (Profitability × 0.18) +
    (Geographic_Diversification × 0.13) +
    (R&D_Productivity × 0.10) +
    (Governance × 0.06) +
    (Valuation × 0.10)
```

For domestic-focused pharma, increase weights on Profitability and Growth, drop Regulatory_Standing to 5%.

#### Pipeline Strength

```
Pipeline = 
    (ANDA_Pending_Score × 0.40) +
    (Complex_Generics_Mix_Score × 0.30) +
    (Specialty_Pipeline_Score × 0.30)

ANDA_Pending_Score: Sector percentile rank of pending ANDAs
```

#### Regulatory Standing (often binary)

```
Regulatory_Score:
    100 = Clean inspection record, no observations
    70  = Form 483 with minor observations
    40  = Warning letter on non-core facility
    0   = Import alert on core facility OR consent decree
```

Inspection outcomes are disclosed via `corporate_announcements`; the `announcement_classifier` should tag these explicitly under a `USFDA_INSPECTION_OUTCOME` category.

#### Pharma Red Flags

| Red Flag | Penalty |
|---|---|
| `USFDA_WARNING_LETTER` (core facility) | −30 |
| `USFDA_WARNING_LETTER` (non-core) | −15 |
| `IMPORT_ALERT` on key facility | −35 |
| `KEY_PRODUCT_PRICE_EROSION` (>15%) | −10 |
| `PATENT_LITIGATION_LOSS` | −15 |
| `PRODUCT_RECALL` | −10 |

