## 7. Technical Layer (Cross-Sector)

The technical score uses the same formula across sectors but weights it differently in the final composite. Inputs come from `nidp.stock_technical_indicators_daily` and `nidp.stock_features_daily`.

```
Technical_Score = 
    (Trend_Score × 0.35) +
    (Relative_Strength × 0.25) +
    (Momentum × 0.20) +
    (Volume_Confirmation × 0.10) +
    (Volatility_Adjusted × 0.10)
```

### Trend Score

```
Trend_Score = 
    (Price > 200DMA ? 30 : 0) +
    (Price > 50DMA ? 25 : 0) +
    (200DMA slope positive over 3M ? 25 : 0) +
    (Price_vs_52W_High_Score × 0.20)

Price_vs_52W_High_Score = MIN(100, MAX(0, ((Price / 52W_High) − 0.75) / 0.25 × 100))
```

### Relative Strength (vs Sector Index)

```
RS_Score = Percentile rank of (Stock 3M return − Sector Index 3M return) within sector

Sector index mapping from sector_master:
    BANK    → Bank Nifty
    NBFC    → Nifty Financial Services
    IT      → Nifty IT
    FMCG    → Nifty FMCG
    PHARMA  → Nifty Pharma
    AUTO    → Nifty Auto
    METAL   → Nifty Metal
    DEFAULT → Nifty 500
```

Source: `nidp.index_close`

### Momentum

```
Momentum = 
    (RSI_Score × 0.40) +
    (MACD_Score × 0.30) +
    (Price_ROC_Score × 0.30)

RSI_Score (sweet spot is 50–65):
    100 if RSI ∈ [50, 65]
    Scale to 70 for RSI ∈ [40,50] or [65,75]
    30 for RSI ∈ [30,40] or [75,80]
    0  if RSI < 30 (deeply oversold — capitulation) or > 80 (overbought)

MACD_Score:
    100 if MACD line > Signal line AND histogram rising
    50  if MACD line > Signal line but histogram flat/falling
    25  if MACD line < Signal line but histogram rising (early reversal)
    0   if both negative and falling
```

### Volume Confirmation (uses delivery %)

```
Volume_Confirmation = 
    (Delivery_Pct_Score × 0.50) +
    (Volume_vs_30D_Avg_Score × 0.30) +
    (OBV_Trend_Score × 0.20)

Delivery_Pct_Score = HIB(Delivery%, floor=30, ceiling=70)
```

The `nidp.delivery` feed gives a powerful edge here — high delivery % means real accumulation, not intraday speculation.

### Volatility Adjustment

```
Volatility_Adjusted = LIB(90D_Realized_Vol%, floor=15, ceiling=50)

Penalizes stocks with extreme volatility — they may have momentum but high tail risk.
```

