## 8. Event-Based Score Overlays

This is where the AI layer (`announcement_classifier` + `event_analyzer`) adds material value beyond pure quantitative scoring.

The `nidp.corporate_event_signals` table contains scored events; the `v3_scores_engine` should overlay these on a 7-day decaying window:

### 8.1 Positive Event Boosts (additive, max +15)

| Event Category (from event_analyzer) | Boost | Decay Period |
|---|---|---|
| `EARNINGS_BEAT` (>10% above estimate) | +8 | 30 days |
| `ACQUISITION_VALUE_ACCRETIVE` | +6 | 60 days |
| `MAJOR_ORDER_WIN` (>5% of revenue) | +5 | 45 days |
| `BUYBACK_ANNOUNCEMENT` (>2% of equity) | +4 | 90 days |
| `INSTITUTIONAL_BULK_BUY` (from bulk_deals + block_deals) | +3 | 14 days |
| `CREDIT_RATING_UPGRADE` | +5 | 90 days |

### 8.2 Negative Event Penalties (additive, max −30)

| Event Category | Penalty | Decay Period |
|---|---|---|
| `EARNINGS_MISS` (>10% below estimate) | −8 | 30 days |
| `AUDITOR_RESIGNATION` | −15 | 180 days |
| `SEBI_ORDER` against company | −20 | 365 days |
| `KEY_MANAGEMENT_EXIT` without succession | −10 | 90 days |
| `PROMOTER_PLEDGE_INCREASE` >10% | −10 | 90 days |
| `INSTITUTIONAL_BULK_SELL` (from bulk_deals) | −5 | 14 days |
| `CREDIT_RATING_DOWNGRADE` | −10 | 180 days |
| `RELATED_PARTY_TRANSACTION_FLAG` | −8 | 90 days |

### 8.3 Decay Formula

```
Effective_Overlay = Raw_Overlay × MAX(0, 1 − (Days_Since_Event / Decay_Period))
```

Implementation note: the `v3_scores_engine` should query `corporate_event_signals` joined with `corporate_announcements` for last 180 days, compute decayed overlays, and apply min/max bounds.

