## 9. Composite V3 Score Assembly

The final assembly per stock:

```
Final_V3_Score = MIN(100, MAX(0,
    (Fundamental × Sector_Fund_Weight) + 
    (Technical × Sector_Tech_Weight) +
    (Cycle_Position × Sector_Cycle_Weight) +   -- 0 for non-cyclicals
    Event_Overlay −                             -- net positive/negative from §8
    Red_Flag_Penalty
))
```

### 9.1 Sector Weight Table

| Sector | Fund_Weight | Tech_Weight | Cycle_Weight |
|---|---|---|---|
| `BANK` | 0.70 | 0.30 | — |
| `NBFC` | 0.70 | 0.30 | — |
| `CYCLICAL` | 0.50 | 0.30 | 0.20 |
| `IT` | 0.70 | 0.30 | — |
| `FMCG` | 0.75 | 0.25 | — |
| `PHARMA` | 0.70 | 0.30 | — |
| `CAPGOODS` | 0.60 | 0.40 | — |
| `DEFAULT` | 0.65 | 0.35 | — |

### 9.2 Score Bands (Buy/Hold/Sell)

Bands are **sector-relative** (top quartile within sector matters more than absolute score, since FMCG quality scores typically run higher than capital goods):

| Band | Definition | Copilot Action |
|---|---|---|
| `STRONG_BUY` | Score ≥ 80 AND in sector top decile | Surfaced as primary recommendation |
| `BUY` | Score ≥ 65 AND in sector top quartile | Eligible for recommendation |
| `HOLD` | Score 50–64 OR sector 2nd quartile | Hold current; no new buy |
| `REDUCE` | Score 35–49 OR red flags present | Suggest trim |
| `AVOID` | Score < 35 OR `AVOID_TRIGGERS` (PCA, import alert, auditor resignation) | Block from recommendations |

### 9.3 Persistence to `nidp.v3_stock_scores_daily`

```sql
INSERT INTO nidp.v3_stock_scores_daily (
    score_date, symbol, sector_profile,
    fundamental_score, technical_score, cycle_position_score,
    event_overlay, red_flag_penalty,
    sub_scores_jsonb, final_score, band
) VALUES (...)
ON CONFLICT (score_date, symbol) DO UPDATE SET ...;
```

The `sub_scores_jsonb` enables the copilot to answer "why did this stock score 72?" with a structured breakdown.

